criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

1. Adults ages 25-65;
2. Self-reported sleep duration \<7 hours per night;
3. Elevated cardiometabolic risk, i.e., presence of one or more of the following - hypertension, obesity, hyperlipidemia, diabetes;
4. Sleep is a behavioral target that individual wants to improve;
5. Complete eligibility screening procedures: Insomnia Severity Index (ISI-7), STOP-BANG, Epworth Sleepiness Scale (ESS);
6. Access to a smartphone, capable of receiving text messages and text links;
7. Able to speak and read English;
8. Willing and able to provide informed consent and participate in all study procedures

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Exceeds eligibility screening thresholds: ISI-7 score ≥22, STOP-BANG score ≥5, ESS score ≥11;
2. Unable to complete study procedures in English;
3. No access to mobile phone with text messaging features;
4. Pregnancy
